 "verdict": "the dipole survives every measured covariate and lives in the best-determined members: it is strong in bound orbits (gap +0.23) and perihelion-spanning arcs (+0.23) but absent in hyperbolic and one-sided-arc members (+0.01, +0.07), directionally positive in every major survey once the hyperbolic dilution is removed, and stable under leave-one-year-out -- a longitude-organized structure of the modern fit record itself, resolved rather than generated by orbit quality (H-RES)"
